== 14. Final host sweep, and the one thing it caught

    The cheap gate list was run on this tree with the repository's own runner, which
    reads the `gates=()` array out of `scripts/verify-in-docker.sh` rather than a copy:

    $ bash scripts/verify-gates.sh
    ...
    all gates passed on the host (27 run, 4 skipped)
    rc=0

    The four skips are the build gates (`cargo check`, `cargo clippy`, `cargo test`,
    GUI protocol types), which `--with-build` runs and which the container run in
    section 9 covers. `cargo fmt --all -- --check` is one of the 27 and passed.

    The first pass of this sweep failed, and it was a true positive, not noise:

      FAIL  TODO status doc (exit 1)
      AssertionError: classify-open-todos: todo-open-items.tsv is stale --
        14 of 137 exported lines differ from TODO.md

    The export carries a TODO.md line number per row, so every line inserted into a
    maintenance section above an open row shifts the rows below it and makes the
    committed export wrong by that amount. The gate reported exactly that, and the fix
    was to regenerate, not to edit the export:

    $ python3 scripts/ci/classify-open-todos.py --write-export docs/verification/todo-open-items.tsv
    classify-open-todos: updated docs/verification/todo-open-items.tsv
    $ python3 scripts/ci/test-classify-open-todos.py
    Ran 14 tests ... OK

    What to keep: an export keyed by line numbers has to be the last thing written in a
    session that edits `TODO.md`, and a `--check-export` run placed before the final
    prose edit proves nothing. This is the same failure shape as section 12a -- a check
    that passed at a moment that was not the moment being shipped.
